invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_mont64_sums
reason: a round of rsa_mont64_mont_mul hands the first of its two steps
  both carries, added in one 64-bit sum. Two carries can pass 2^64, so
  that sum wraps for some operands. rsa_mont64_sums runs the function
  with --unsigned-overflow-check on, where that sum is a property.

--- old
            rsa_mont64_sum ab_sum = rsa_mont64_mul_add_add(*a_word, b[j], t[j], ab_carry);
--- new
            rsa_mont64_sum ab_sum =
                rsa_mont64_mul_add_add(*a_word, b[j], t[j], ab_carry + um_carry);
